<section class="kaffarah-guide three-tool-knowledge" id="kaffarah-guide" aria-labelledby="kaffarah-guide-heading">
 <h2 id="kaffarah-guide-heading">Kaffarah calculator guide: broken oaths, Ramadan and expiation remedies</h2>
 <p><strong>Short answer:</strong> There is <strong>no single universal Kaffarah amount</strong>. For deliberate broken oaths, <a href="https://quran.com/5/89" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Quran 5:89</a> describes feeding or clothing <strong>ten needy people</strong> (or a historically mentioned alternative), with <strong>three days of fasting</strong> if unable. <a href="https://sunnah.com/bukhari:1936" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Sahih al-Bukhari 1936</a> concerns a <em>different</em>, specific Ramadan intercourse case and includes <strong>two successive months of fasting</strong> and <strong>feeding sixty people</strong> in its sequence. The correct remedy depends on a qualified assessment of the facts.</p>
